ta/LBool.html#Lean.LBool\">Lean.LBool</a></span></span>)</span> → <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Data/BudgetedCache.html#Lean.BudgetedBEq\">Lean.BudgetedBEq</a> <span class=\"fn\">α</span></span></span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Lean/Data/BudgetedCache.html#Lean.BudgetedBEq.mk","kind":"ctor","line":17,"name":"Lean.BudgetedBEq.mk","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Data/BudgetedCache.lean#L17-L23"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">class</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Data/BudgetedCache.html#Lean.BudgetedBEq\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">BudgetedBEq</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u</div></div>","info":{"doc":"Equality for cache keys with a work budget. `.undef` means the comparison exhausted its budget.\nThe comparison may break referential transparency by depending on pointer sharing, so it runs\nin `BaseIO`. A definite result must agree with the key's intended equality.","docLink":"./Lean/Data/BudgetedCache.html#Lean.BudgetedBEq","kind":"class","line":17,"name":"Lean.BudgetedBEq","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Data/BudgetedCache.lean#L17-L23"}}],"imports":["Init.System.IO","Lean.Data.LBool","Lean.Data.PersistentHashMap"],"instances":[{"className":"Inhabited","name":"Lean.instInhabitedBudgetedCache","typeNames":["Lean.BudgetedCache"]},{"className":"EmptyCollection","name":"Lean.BudgetedCache.instEmptyCollection","typeNames":["Lean.BudgetedCache"]}],"name":"Lean.Data.BudgetedCache"}